  <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="HHFB845F6A13C048AB10E053139FD9FDD6" contextRef="HH6F430EA68AFC29D1DD829B0DDD45FFF4">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basis of Accounting&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpine Transportation Company is subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (FERC).?The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements generally conform to those required by FERC.&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounting for Partner Capital&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Alpine Transportation Company is organized as a partnership under the partnership laws of the State of Alaska. Partnerships do not have capital stock and retained income, but rather combine partner capital and undistributed earnings as Partner Capital.&amp;#160;In the absence of Partner Capital account in the Uniform System of Accounts, Partner Capital and undistributed earnings are captured in FERC account 70, Capital Stock.&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Page 119, Unappropriated Retained Income Statement is not included in the financial reports provided because there is not a balance in Account 75, Unappropriated Retained Income, which Page 119 supports.&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Page 700 Not Included with this Submission&amp;#160;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Page 700 is not included with this report as it is not required.?Pipelines comprising the Trans-Alaska Pipeline System (TAPS) and any pipeline delivering oil directly or indirectly into the TAPS are excluded from Page 700 reporting requirements.&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
